<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Resize</h1>
<p>Skill
Taught by the craftsmen of Midgaard, to anyone: Tom the Tailor (resize clothes), Myrna the Leather Worker (resize leather) and Sam the Blacksmith (resize metal)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>resize &lt;item&gt;
resize &lt;item&gt; &lt;person&gt;
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>resize boots
resize boots eve
</pre>
<p>Alters something worn or wielded to fit a different size of person: 
yourself, or the person you name. Armour, clothes and weapons are made for 
someone's height, and don't fit everyone.
</p><p>Which of the three skills you need depends on the item: clothes and 
cloth for resize clothes, leather armour for resize leather, and chain, 
plate, shields, weapons and anything else for resize metal. Clothes take 
dexterity, leather and metal take strength.
</p><p>The bigger the change, and the finer the item, the harder the job and the 
more endurance it takes; shrinking is easier than enlarging. An item can 
be resized only once. Fail, and nothing happens; fail badly, and you 
damage the item, or even destroy it. You must be standing.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
